{"id": "EUVD-2026-59338", "enisaUuid": "d85a8a05-e4f3-30e5-8d16-d7b6d2acee5f", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmd/raid10: fix writes_pending leak on write request failures\n\nraid10_make_request() acquires a writes_pending reference with\nmd_write_start() before dispatching write requests. Several failure\npaths in raid10_write_request() complete the bio and return without\nreaching the normal write completion path, causing the corresponding\nmd_write_end() to be skipped.\n\nMake raid10_write_request() return a status indicating whether the write\nrequest was successfully queued. This allows raid10_make_request() to\nrelease the writes_pending reference with md_write_end() when a write\nrequest fails.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:56:52", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:44:56", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f076460c5205c9687059e5a3afeed37d2f2ceb6b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b6667d925c274910423385042edf18f6788dbceb", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c642583adc136d4c70ce3c65c3f43e847d26c776", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f94031c94eaebe14a7c9e91720064de0c5a54a6c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/e045d6ed33f8faa3e3dd6dc33c62ec01e3ad275d"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-72439", "GHSA-xqj6-523w-5f3g"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0e716b40-6ee3-3bd0-8f89-a56f4af4a86a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.17"}, {"id": "15a04ad3-3303-3edd-b893-16b5360e44a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <c642583adc136d4c70ce3c65c3f43e847d26c776"}, {"id": "27bff427-c290-31fd-9600-773b8a13dcae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "2b9d7188-2e43-3a45-8583-0b48bb4d3d44", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <b6667d925c274910423385042edf18f6788dbceb"}, {"id": "32fed56c-544d-38d1-bea7-37d2460fa6ec", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "434ec9a0-04d2-391f-b6d3-00193a556e42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <f076460c5205c9687059e5a3afeed37d2f2ceb6b"}, {"id": "54f2e852-0493-340d-8195-fc8e1c73239b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <e045d6ed33f8faa3e3dd6dc33c62ec01e3ad275d"}, {"id": "8a675753-d3f2-32fe-9a47-de7f034cf0fe", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "8cbdf967-4756-3ff1-9cf1-fa09bc2a92f2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "c9aa889b035fca4598ae985a0f0c76ebbb547ad2 <f94031c94eaebe14a7c9e91720064de0c5a54a6c"}, {"id": "b6b13742-b598-39b7-8af4-0f1b5f042842", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "b6f4a5cb-b1bb-3a01-8240-5fc0f37e5e3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "39db562b3fedb93978a7e42dd216b306740959f8"}, {"id": "bb88331d-6039-30b0-b11b-38d0aef0f996", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "ce37b430-32cb-33f6-aee4-e9c0b4150520", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.15.111 <5.16"}, {"id": "ea5d275c-edfb-388c-bfa6-a7fd6b8c4e86", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8c473a00-3416-3d97-9e07-ca51e3e25593", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}